AT S1E1W updates PAR_EL1 only after a context synchronization event: mmu_kvtop_wpreflight reads it after an ISB, as mmu_kvtop does.
A fix to Apple's xnu (APSL 2.0 like this series), taken from UniXNU's patches/xnu-12377/native-at-par-sync.patch at f65660d (github.com/UniXNU/UniXNU,
BSD-2-Clause-Patent; commit by bluseliu50, 8 November 2026): the one added line is theirs. Not behind SCION_NATIVE_PAC: the ISB is architecturally required.
Their licence notice: patches/xnu-12377/LICENSE.UniXNU.

diff --git a/osfmk/arm64/machine_routines_asm.s b/osfmk/arm64/machine_routines_asm.s
index d5fe8bf..9e66622 100644
--- a/osfmk/arm64/machine_routines_asm.s
+++ b/osfmk/arm64/machine_routines_asm.s
@@ -465,6 +465,7 @@ LEXT(mmu_kvtop_wpreflight)
 	mrs		x2, DAIF									// Load current DAIF
 	msr		DAIFSet, #(DAIFSC_STANDARD_DISABLE)		// Disable all asynchronous exceptions
 	at		s1e1w, x0									// Translation Stage 1 EL1
+	isb		sy											// PAR_EL1 holds the result only after a context synchronization, as in mmu_kvtop
 	mrs		x1, PAR_EL1									// Read result
 	msr		DAIF, x2									// Restore interrupt state
 	tbnz	x1, #0, L_mmu_kvtop_wpreflight_invalid		// Test Translation not valid
